{
  "_about": [
    "Ground truth for the package images in test-data/images/.",
    "",
    "Values are written in the NORMALISED form the extractor is expected to",
    "produce, not verbatim as printed: prices as '₹<amount>', quantities as",
    "'<number> <standard unit>', packing dates as 'MM/YYYY'. Manufacturer and",
    "consumer-care are scored as a substring match, because there are several",
    "defensible ways to crop a name or a contact off a pack and none of them is",
    "wrong.",
    "",
    "null means the declaration is genuinely NOT READABLE in this frame. That",
    "covers two different situations and the distinction matters:",
    "  - not printed on the pack at all (a real compliance finding)",
    "  - printed, but on a panel this photograph does not show (a framing problem)",
    "'absent_reason' records which, so accuracy is not measured against something",
    "the recogniser could never have seen.",
    "",
    "Verify any entry marked 'uncertain' against the physical pack before trusting",
    "it as a benchmark.",
    "A declaration may list several lawful values - a phone and an email for consumer care, a packer and a marketer for the maker. Where the pack does, 'expected' is an array and any member counts as correct."
  ],
